; Specification: 3GPP TS 29.214
; Version: 18.4.0
; Vendor-ID: 10415
; Bases: RFC6733
; Link: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/129200_129299/129214/18.04.00_60/ts_129214v180400p.pdf


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-ue-address)
; AVP: Framed-IP-Address
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 15
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AF shall provide the full IP address of the UE using either Framed-IP-Address AVP or Framed-Ipv6-Prefix AVP, and the corresponding Service Information within Media-Component-Description AVP(s)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aaa-access-network-charging-identifier)
; AVP: Access-Network-Charging-Identifier
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 15
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The acknowledgement towards the AF should take place before or in parallel with any required PCC Rule provisioning towards the PCEF and shall include the Access-Network-Charging-Identifier(s) and may include the Access-Network-Charging-Address AVP, if they are available."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aaa-an-gw-address)
; AVP: AN-GW-Address
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 15
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AA-Answer message shall also include the AN-GW-Address AVP, if the PCRF has previously requested to be updated with this information in the PCEF."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aaa-sgsn-mcc-mnc)
; AVP: 3GPP-SGSN-MCC-MNC
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 15
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AA-Answer message shall also include the PLMN identifier within the 3GPP-SGSN-MCC-MNC AVP if the PCRF has previously requested to be updated with this information in the PCEF/BBERF."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aaa-ip-can-type)
; AVP: IP-CAN-Type
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 15
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AA-Answer message shall also include the IP-CAN-Type AVP. if the PCRF has previously requested to be updated with this information in the PCEF/BBERF."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aaa-rat-type)
; AVP: RAT-Type
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 15
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"In that case, the AA-Answer message shall also include the RAT type information within the RAT-Type AVP and AN-Trusted AVP when applicable for the specific IP-CAN Type."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-reservation-priority-default)
; AVP: Reservation-Priority
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 15
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"If the Reservation-Priority AVP is not specified the requested priority is DEFAULT (0)."
    default DEFAULT


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aaa-retry-interval)
; AVP: Retry-Interval
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 15
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"When the AF receives the re-try interval within the Retry-Interval AVP, the AF shall not send the same service information to the PCRF again (for the same IP-CAN session) until the re-try interval has elapsed."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-after-acknowledgement)
; AVP: Session-Id
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.2
; Page: 20
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AF shall send an AA-Request command to the PCRF, only after the previous AA-Request has been acknowledged."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#sta-used-service-unit)
; AVP: Sponsored-Connectivity-Data
; Command: ST-Answer
; Section: 4.4.4
; Page: 24
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The PCRF shall send then the ST-Answer to the AF including the Used-Service-Unit AVP for reporting accumulated usage within the Sponsored-Connectivity-Data AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#sta-access-network-information)
; AVP: 3GPP-User-Location-Info
; Command: ST-Answer
; Section: 4.4.4
; Page: 24
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The PCRF shall send then the ST-Answer to the AF including the required data within the 3GPP-User-Location-Info AVP (if available), TWAN-Identifier AVP (if available), User-Location-Info-Time AVP (if available), UE-Local-IP-Address AVP (if available), UDP-Source-Port AVP (if available), TCP-Source-Port AVP (if available), 3GPP-SGSN-MCC-MNC AVP (if location info is not available) and/or 3GPP-MS-TimeZone AVP (if available)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#sta-ran-nas-release-cause)
; AVP: RAN-NAS-Release-Cause
; Command: ST-Answer
; Section: 4.4.4
; Page: 24
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"Additionally, if the PCRF received from the PCEF the RAN cause and/or NAS cause, TWAN cause or untrusted WLAN cause, the PCRF shall provide the received cause(s) in the RAN-NAS-Release-Cause AVP in the ST-Answer command."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#rar-usage-report-used-service-unit)
; AVP: Sponsored-Connectivity-Data
; Command: RA-Request
; Section: 4.4.6.6
; Page: 27
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"When the PCRF detects that the usage threshold has been reached or the AF disables the sponsored data connectivity, the PCRF shall report the accumulated usage as provided by the PCEF/TDF to the AF in a RA-Request (RAR) command with the Specific-Action AVP set to the value USAGE_REPORT; Otherwise, when the AF session is terminated by the AF or the PCRF, the PCRF shall report the accumulated usage as provided by the PCEF/TDF to the AF in ST-Answer (STA) command."
"The accumulated usage shall be reported in the Used-Service-Unit AVP within the Sponsored-Connectivity-Data AVP."
    present-if Specific-Action = USAGE_REPORT
    absent-if Specific-Action = USAGE_REPORT and not Sponsored-Connectivity-Data/Used-Service-Unit


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#rar-access-network-info-report)
; AVP: 3GPP-User-Location-Info
; Command: RA-Request
; Section: 4.4.6.7
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"If the information is provided in the RAR command, PCRF shall also provide the ACCESS_NETWORK_INFO_REPORT within Specific-Action AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-access-network-info-required-access-info)
; AVP: Required-Access-Info
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.6.7
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"If the AF requests the PCRF to report the access network information (i.e. user location and/or user timezone information), the AF shall subscribe to the \"ACCESS_NETWORK_INFO_REPORT\" within the Specific-Action AVP and shall include the required access network information within the Required-Access-Info AVP."
    present-if Specific-Action = ACCESS_NETWORK_INFO_REPORT


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-restoration-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.7
; Page: 29
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AF shall also include the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1) in the AAR command, as described in IETF RFC 6733 [52]."
    present-if Rx-Request-Type = PCSCF_RESTORATION
    values 1 if Rx-Request-Type = PCSCF_RESTORATION


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-restoration-subscription-id)
; AVP: Subscription-Id
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.7
; Page: 29
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The P-CSCF acting as AF shall send an AAR command including the Rx-Request-Type AVP set to the value PCSCF_RESTORATION (2) to the PCRF in the case P-CSCF Restoration needs to be performed."
"If the IP address is not available or if the IP address is not unique and the IP-Domain-ID is not available, the P-CSCF shall include the IMSI in the Subscription-Id AVP and the APN in the Called-Station-Id AVP."
    present-if Rx-Request-Type = PCSCF_RESTORATION and not Framed-IP-Address and not Framed-IPv6-Prefix


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-restoration-called-station-id)
; AVP: Called-Station-Id
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.7
; Page: 29
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The P-CSCF acting as AF shall send an AAR command including the Rx-Request-Type AVP set to the value PCSCF_RESTORATION (2) to the PCRF in the case P-CSCF Restoration needs to be performed."
"If the IP address is not available or if the IP address is not unique and the IP-Domain-ID is not available, the P-CSCF shall include the IMSI in the Subscription-Id AVP and the APN in the Called-Station-Id AVP."
    present-if Rx-Request-Type = PCSCF_RESTORATION and not Framed-IP-Address and not Framed-IPv6-Prefix


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aaa-restoration-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.7
; Page: 29
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The PCRF shall acknowledge the AAR command by sending an AAA command to the P-CSCF acting as AF and shall include the Auth-Session-State AVP set to NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1)."
    present-if request/Rx-Request-Type = PCSCF_RESTORATION and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
    values 1 if request/Rx-Request-Type = PCSCF_RESTORATION and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-restoration-imsi)
; AVP: Framed-IP-Address
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.7
; Page: 29
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The P-CSCF acting as AF shall send an AAR command including the Rx-Request-Type AVP set to the value PCSCF_RESTORATION (2) to the PCRF in the case P-CSCF Restoration needs to be performed."
"If the IP address is not available or if the IP address is not unique and the IP-Domain-ID is not available, the P-CSCF shall include the IMSI in the Subscription-Id AVP and the APN in the Called-Station-Id AVP."
    present-if Rx-Request-Type = PCSCF_RESTORATION and not Framed-IPv6-Prefix and not Subscription-Id/Subscription-Id-Type = END_USER_IMSI


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#rar-flows-content-versions)
; AVP: Content-Version
; Within: Flows
; Section: 4.4.9
; Page: 30
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The PCRF shall include more than one Content-Version AVPs for the same media component within the Flows AVP in a RAR command if it has received multiple content versions as described in clause 4.5.28 or clause 4a.5.18 in 3GPP TS 29.212 [8]."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#extended-max-requested-bw-dl-range)
; AVP: Extended-Max-Requested-BW-DL
; Section: 4.4.10
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"For values lower or equal to 2^32-1 bps AVPs representing bitrates in bps shall be used."
    range 4294968..*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#extended-max-requested-bw-ul-range)
; AVP: Extended-Max-Requested-BW-UL
; Section: 4.4.10
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"For values lower or equal to 2^32-1 bps AVPs representing bitrates in bps shall be used."
    range 4294968..*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#extended-max-supported-bw-dl-range)
; AVP: Extended-Max-Supported-BW-DL
; Section: 4.4.10
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"For values lower or equal to 2^32-1 bps AVPs representing bitrates in bps shall be used."
    range 4294968..*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#extended-max-supported-bw-ul-range)
; AVP: Extended-Max-Supported-BW-UL
; Section: 4.4.10
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"For values lower or equal to 2^32-1 bps AVPs representing bitrates in bps shall be used."
    range 4294968..*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#extended-min-desired-bw-dl-range)
; AVP: Extended-Min-Desired-BW-DL
; Section: 4.4.10
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"For values lower or equal to 2^32-1 bps AVPs representing bitrates in bps shall be used."
    range 4294968..*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#extended-min-desired-bw-ul-range)
; AVP: Extended-Min-Desired-BW-UL
; Section: 4.4.10
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"For values lower or equal to 2^32-1 bps AVPs representing bitrates in bps shall be used."
    range 4294968..*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#extended-min-requested-bw-dl-range)
; AVP: Extended-Min-Requested-BW-DL
; Section: 4.4.10
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"For values lower or equal to 2^32-1 bps AVPs representing bitrates in bps shall be used."
    range 4294968..*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#extended-min-requested-bw-ul-range)
; AVP: Extended-Min-Requested-BW-UL
; Section: 4.4.10
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"For values lower or equal to 2^32-1 bps AVPs representing bitrates in bps shall be used."
    range 4294968..*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#establishment-bandwidth-upper-limit)
; AVP: Max-Requested-Bandwidth-DL
; Section: 4.4.10
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"When the Rx session is being established, if the AF supports the corresponding feature (as listed above) and needs to indicate bandwidth values higher than 2^32-1 bps, AVPs representing bitrate in bps shall be provided with value set to 2^32-1 bps and bandwidth AVPs representing bitrate in kbps shall be provided with the actual required bandwidth."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-mps-signalling-mps-identifier)
; AVP: MPS-Identifier
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.12
; Page: 32
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"To provision the AF signalling flow information, the AF shall provide the UE’s IP address using either Framed-IP-Address AVP or Framed-Ipv6-Prefix AVP. The AF shall additionally provide the MPS-Identifier AVP and a Media-Component-Description AVP containing a Media-Component-Number AVP set to \"0\", and including a Media-Sub-Component AVP that contains the Flow-Description AVP set to the AF signalling IP flow. If the AuthorizationForMpsSignalling feature is supported, the AF shall provide the MPS-Action AVP set to value AUTHORIZE_AND_ENABLE_MPS_FOR_AF_SIGNALLING (3)."
    present-if MPS-Action = AUTHORIZE_AND_ENABLE_MPS_FOR_AF_SIGNALLING


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-mps-signalling-media-component)
; AVP: Media-Component-Description
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.12
; Page: 32
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"To provision the AF signalling flow information, the AF shall provide the UE’s IP address using either Framed-IP-Address AVP or Framed-Ipv6-Prefix AVP. The AF shall additionally provide the MPS-Identifier AVP and a Media-Component-Description AVP containing a Media-Component-Number AVP set to \"0\", and including a Media-Sub-Component AVP that contains the Flow-Description AVP set to the AF signalling IP flow. If the AuthorizationForMpsSignalling feature is supported, the AF shall provide the MPS-Action AVP set to value AUTHORIZE_AND_ENABLE_MPS_FOR_AF_SIGNALLING (3)."
    present-if MPS-Action = AUTHORIZE_AND_ENABLE_MPS_FOR_AF_SIGNALLING


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-mps-signalling-framed-ip-address)
; AVP: Framed-IP-Address
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.12
; Page: 32
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"To provision the AF signalling flow information, the AF shall provide the UE’s IP address using either Framed-IP-Address AVP or Framed-Ipv6-Prefix AVP. The AF shall additionally provide the MPS-Identifier AVP and a Media-Component-Description AVP containing a Media-Component-Number AVP set to \"0\", and including a Media-Sub-Component AVP that contains the Flow-Description AVP set to the AF signalling IP flow. If the AuthorizationForMpsSignalling feature is supported, the AF shall provide the MPS-Action AVP set to value AUTHORIZE_AND_ENABLE_MPS_FOR_AF_SIGNALLING (3)."
    present-if MPS-Action = AUTHORIZE_AND_ENABLE_MPS_FOR_AF_SIGNALLING and not Framed-IPv6-Prefix


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-mps-signalling-flow)
; AVP: MPS-Action
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.4.12
; Page: 32
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AF shall additionally provide the MPS-Identifier AVP and a Media-Component-Description AVP containing a Media-Component-Number AVP set to \"0\", and including a Media-Sub-Component AVP that contains the Flow-Description AVP set to the AF signalling IP flow."
    requires not MPS-Action = AUTHORIZE_AND_ENABLE_MPS_FOR_AF_SIGNALLING or Media-Component-Description/Media-Component-Number = 0 and Media-Component-Description/Media-Sub-Component/Flow-Description


; Type: Application Scope
; Name: Rx
; Section: 5.1
; Page: 33
; Application-ID: 16777236
; Applies-To: 5.*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#auth-application-id-rx)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Section: 5.1
; Page: 33
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"Tthe Rx application identification shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP."
    range 16777236


; Type: Message
; Name: AA-Request, AAR
; Section: 5.6.1
; Page: 69
<AA-Request> ::= < Diameter Header: 265, REQ, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Auth-Application-Id }
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        { Destination-Realm }
        [ Destination-Host ]
        [ IP-Domain-Id ]
        [ Auth-Session-State ]
        [ AF-Application-Identifier ]   ; bold
      * [ Media-Component-Description ] ; bold
        [ Service-Info-Status ]         ; bold
        [ AF-Charging-Identifier ]      ; bold
        [ SIP-Forking-Indication ]      ; bold
      * [ Specific-Action ]             ; bold
      * [ Subscription-Id ]             ; bold
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]       ; bold
      * [ Supported-Features ]          ; bold
        [ Reservation-Priority ]        ; bold
        [ Framed-IP-Address ]           ; bold
        [ Framed-IPv6-Prefix ]          ; bold ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#aar-framed-ipv6-prefix-case)
        [ Called-Station-Id ]           ; bold
        [ Service-URN ]                 ; bold
        [ Sponsored-Connectivity-Data ] ; bold
        [ MPS-Identifier ]              ; bold
        [ GCS-Identifier ]              ; bold
        [ MCPTT-Identifier ]            ; bold
        [ MCVideo-Identifier ]          ; bold
        [ IMS-Content-Identifier ]      ; bold
        [ IMS-Content-Type ]            ; bold
      * [ Calling-Party-Address ]       ; bold
        [ Callee-Information ]          ; bold
        [ Rx-Request-Type ]             ; bold
      * [ Required-Access-Info ]        ; bold
        [ AF-Requested-Data ]           ; bold
        [ Reference-Id ]                ; bold
        [ Pre-emption-Control-Info ]    ; bold
        [ MPS-Action ]                  ; bold
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: AA-Answer, AAA
; Section: 5.6.2
; Page: 70
<AA-Answer> ::= < Diameter Header: 265, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Auth-Application-Id }
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        [ Result-Code ]
        [ Experimental-Result ]
        [ Auth-Session-State ]
      * [ Access-Network-Charging-Identifier ] ; bold
        [ Access-Network-Charging-Address ]    ; bold
        [ Acceptable-Service-Info ]            ; bold
     *2 [ AN-GW-Address ]                      ; bold
        [ AN-Trusted ]                         ; bold
        [ Service-Authorization-Info ]         ; bold
        [ IP-CAN-Type ]                        ; bold
        [ MA-Information ]                     ; bold
        [ NetLoc-Access-Support ]              ; bold
        [ RAT-Type ]
      * [ Flows ]                              ; bold
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]              ; bold
        [ OC-OLR ]                             ; bold
      * [ Supported-Features ]
      * [ Subscription-Id ]
        [ User-Equipment-Info ]
        [ User-Equipment-Info-Extension ]
        [ 3GPP-SGSN-MCC-MNC ]
        [ NID ]
      * [ Class ]
        [ Error-Message ]
        [ Error-Reporting-Host ]
        [ Failed-AVP ]
        [ Retry-Interval ]                     ; bold
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
      * [ Redirect-Host ]
        [ Redirect-Host-Usage ]
        [ Redirect-Max-Cache-Time ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Load ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: RA-Request, RAR
; Section: 5.6.3
; Page: 70
<RA-Request> ::= < Diameter Header: 258, REQ, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        { Destination-Realm }
        { Destination-Host }
        { Auth-Application-Id }
      * { Specific-Action }
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]              ; bold
      * [ Access-Network-Charging-Identifier ] ; bold
        [ Access-Network-Charging-Address ]    ; bold
     *2 [ AN-GW-Address ]                      ; bold
        [ AN-Trusted ]                         ; bold
      * [ Flows ]                              ; bold
      * [ Subscription-Id ]                    ; bold
        [ Abort-Cause ]                        ; bold
        [ IP-CAN-Type ]                        ; bold
        [ MA-Information ]                     ; bold
        [ NetLoc-Access-Support ]              ; bold
        [ RAT-Type ]                           ; bold
        [ Sponsored-Connectivity-Data ]        ; bold
        [ 3GPP-User-Location-Info ]            ; bold
        [ User-Location-Info-Time ]            ; bold
        [ 3GPP-MS-TimeZone ]                   ; bold
      * [ RAN-NAS-Release-Cause ]              ; bold
      * [ 5GS-RAN-NAS-Release-Cause ]          ; bold
        [ 3GPP-SGSN-MCC-MNC ]                  ; bold
        [ NID ]                                ; bold
        [ TWAN-Identifier ]                    ; bold
        [ TCP-Source-Port ]                    ; bold
        [ UDP-Source-Port ]                    ; bold
        [ UE-Local-IP-Address ]                ; bold
        [ Wireline-User-Location-Info ]        ; bold
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
      * [ Class ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: RA-Answer, RAA
; Section: 5.6.4
; Page: 71
<RA-Answer> ::= < Diameter Header: 258, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        [ Result-Code ]
        [ Experimental-Result ]
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]       ; bold
        [ OC-OLR ]                      ; bold
      * [ Media-Component-Description ] ; bold
        [ Service-URN ]                 ; bold
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
      * [ Class ]
        [ Error-Message ]
        [ Error-Reporting-Host ]
      * [ Redirect-Host ]
        [ Redirect-Host-Usage ]
        [ Redirect-Max-Cache-Time ]
        [ Failed-AVP ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: ST-Request, STR
; Section: 5.6.5
; Page: 71
<ST-Request> ::= < Diameter Header: 275, REQ, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        { Destination-Realm }
        { Auth-Application-Id }
        { Termination-Cause }
        [ Destination-Host ]
        [ OC-Supported-Features ] ; bold
      * [ Required-Access-Info ]  ; bold
      * [ Class ]
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: ST-Answer, STA
; Section: 5.6.6
; Page: 72
<ST-Answer> ::= < Diameter Header: 275, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        [ Result-Code ]
        [ Error-Message ]
        [ Error-Reporting-Host ]
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]       ; bold
        [ OC-OLR ]                      ; bold
        [ Failed-AVP ]
        [ Sponsored-Connectivity-Data ] ; bold
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
        [ 3GPP-User-Location-Info ]     ; bold
        [ User-Location-Info-Time ]     ; bold
        [ 3GPP-MS-TimeZone ]            ; bold
      * [ RAN-NAS-Release-Cause ]       ; bold
      * [ 5GS-RAN-NAS-Release-Cause ]   ; bold
        [ 3GPP-SGSN-MCC-MNC ]           ; bold
        [ NID ]                         ; bold
        [ TWAN-Identifier ]             ; bold
        [ TCP-Source-Port ]             ; bold
        [ UDP-Source-Port ]             ; bold
        [ UE-Local-IP-Address ]         ; bold
        [ NetLoc-Access-Support ]       ; bold ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#sta-netloc-access-support-case)
        [ Wireline-User-Location-Info ] ; bold
      * [ Class ]
      * [ Redirect-Host ]
        [ Redirect-Host-Usage ]
        [ Redirect-Max-Cache-Time ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Load ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: AS-Request, ASR
; Section: 5.6.7
; Page: 72
<AS-Request> ::= < Diameter Header: 274, REQ, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        { Destination-Realm }
        { Destination-Host }
        { Auth-Application-Id }
        [ OC-Supported-Features ] ; bold
        { Abort-Cause }           ; bold
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: AS-Answer, ASA
; Section: 5.6.8
; Page: 73
<AS-Answer> ::= < Diameter Header: 274, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        [ Result-Code ]
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]   ; bold
        [ OC-OLR ]                  ; bold
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
        [ Error-Message ]
        [ Error-Reporting-Host ]
        [ Failed-AVP ]
      * [ Redirect-Host ]
        [ Redirect-Host-Usage ]
        [ Redirect-Max-Cache-Time ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ AVP ]


