"When used in RAR it indicates that the PCRF generated the request because of an IP-CAN or RAT change. IP-CAN-Type AVP, RAT-Type AVP (if applicable) ,AN-Trusted AVP (if applicable) and AN-GW-Address AVP (if applicable) shall be provided in the same request with the new/valid value(s)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#rar-plmn-change)
; AVP: 3GPP-SGSN-MCC-MNC
; Command: RA-Request
; Section: 5.3.13
; Page: 40
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"In the RA-Request (RAR), this value shall be used by the PCRF to indicate that there was a change of PLMN."
"3GPP-SGSN-MCC-MNC AVP shall be provided in the same RAR command with the new value and, if available, the NID AVP."
    present-if Specific-Action = PLMN_CHANGE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#max-requested-bandwidth-dl-extended)
; AVP: Max-Requested-Bandwidth-DL
; Section: 5.3.14
; Page: 44
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"When the Extended-Max-Requested-BW-NR feature is supported and the value to be transmitted exceeds 2^32-1, the Extended-Max-Requested-Bandwidth-DL AVP shall be used , see clause 4.4.10 and clause 5.3.52."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#max-requested-bandwidth-ul-extended)
; AVP: Max-Requested-Bandwidth-UL
; Section: 5.3.15
; Page: 44
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"When the Extended-Max-Requested-BW-NR feature is supported and the value to be transmitted exceeds 2^32-1, the Extended-Max-Requested-Bandwidth-UL AVP shall be used, see clause 4.4.10 and clause 5.3.53."
    text-only


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Media-Component-Description
; Section: 5.3.16
; Page: 44
Media-Component-Description ::= < AVP header: 517 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#vendor-id-media-component-description)
        { Media-Component-Number }
      * [ Media-Sub-Component ]
        [ AF-Application-Identifier ]
        [ FLUS-Identifier ]
        [ Media-Type ]
        [ Max-Requested-Bandwidth-UL ]
        [ Max-Requested-Bandwidth-DL ]
        [ Max-Supported-Bandwidth-UL ]
        [ Max-Supported-Bandwidth-DL ]
        [ Min-Desired-Bandwidth-UL ]
        [ Min-Desired-Bandwidth-DL ]
        [ Min-Requested-Bandwidth-UL ]
        [ Min-Requested-Bandwidth-DL ]
        [ Extended-Max-Requested-BW-UL ]
        [ Extended-Max-Requested-BW-DL ]
        [ Extended-Max-Supported-BW-UL ]
        [ Extended-Max-Supported-BW-DL ]
        [ Extended-Min-Desired-BW-UL ]
        [ Extended-Min-Desired-BW-DL ]
        [ Extended-Min-Requested-BW-UL ]
        [ Extended-Min-Requested-BW-DL ]
        [ Flow-Status ]
        [ Priority-Sharing-Indicator ]
        [ Pre-emption-Capability ]
        [ Pre-emption-Vulnerability ]
        [ Reservation-Priority ]
        [ RS-Bandwidth ]
        [ RR-Bandwidth ]
     *2 [ Codec-Data ]
        [ Sharing-Key-DL ]
        [ Sharing-Key-UL ]
        [ Content-Version ]
        [ Max-PLR-DL ]
        [ Max-PLR-UL ]
        [ Desired-Max-Latency ]
        [ Desired-Max-Loss ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#media-component-description-single-flow)
; AVP: Media-Component-Description
; Section: 5.3.16
; Page: 44
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"Within one Diameter message, a single IP flow shall not be described by more than one Media-Component-Description AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#media-component-reservation-priority-default)
; AVP: Reservation-Priority
; Within: Media-Component-Description
; Section: 5.3.16
; Page: 44
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"If the Reservation-Priority AVP is not specified the IP flow priority is DEFAULT (0)."
    default DEFAULT


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#media-component-codec-data-offer-answer)
; AVP: Codec-Data
; Within: Media-Component-Description
; Section: 5.3.16
; Page: 44
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"If the Media-Component-Description AVP contains two Codec-Data AVPs, one of them shall represent an SDP offer and the other one the corresponding SDP answer."
    text-only
"If SDP is applied without using the offer-answer procedures, zero or one Codec-Data AVP shall be provisioned."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#acceptable-service-info-media-component)
; AVP: Media-Component-Description
; Within: Acceptable-Service-Info
; Section: 5.3.16
; Page: 44
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The PCRF may provide the Media-Component-Description AVP(s) within the Acceptable-Service-Info AVP in the AA-Answer command if the service information received from the AF is rejected."
"For this usage, the Media-Component-Description AVP shall only include the appropriate Media-Component-Number AVP and the Max-Requested-Bandwidth-UL and/or Max-Requested-Bandwidth-DL AVPs and/ or the Extended-Max-Requested-BW-UL AVP and/or the Extended-Max-Requested-BW-DL AVP (see clause 4.4.10) indicating the maximum acceptable bandwidth."
    members only Media-Component-Number Max-Requested-Bandwidth-UL Max-Requested-Bandwidth-DL Extended-Max-Requested-BW-UL Extended-Max-Requested-BW-DL


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#media-component-number-af-signalling)
; AVP: Media-Component-Number
; Within: Media-Component-Description
; Section: 5.3.17
; Page: 46
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"When this AVP refers to AF signalling, this is indicated by using the value 0 according to the rules in Annex B."
    values 0 if Media-Sub-Component/Flow-Usage = AF_SIGNALLING


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Media-Sub-Component
; Section: 5.3.18
; Page: 46
Media-Sub-Component ::= < AVP header: 519 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#vendor-id-media-sub-component)
        { Flow-Number }
     *2 [ Flow-Description ]
        [ Flow-Status ]
        [ Flow-Usage ]
        [ Max-Requested-Bandwidth-UL ]
        [ Max-Requested-Bandwidth-DL ]
        [ Extended-Max-Requested-BW-UL ]
        [ Extended-Max-Requested-BW-DL ]
        [ AF-Signalling-Protocol ]
        [ ToS-Traffic-Class ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#media-sub-component-af-signalling-protocol)
; AVP: AF-Signalling-Protocol
; Within: Media-Sub-Component
; Section: 5.3.18
; Page: 46
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AF-Signalling-Protocol AVP may be included only if the Flow-Usage AVP has a value of ‘AF_SIGNALLING’."
    requires Flow-Usage = AF_SIGNALLING


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Media-Type
; Section: 5.3.19
; Page: 47
Media-Type ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 520 10415 >
        AUDIO       = 0
        VIDEO       = 1
        DATA        = 2
        APPLICATION = 3
        CONTROL     = 4
        TEXT        = 5
        MESSAGE     = 6
        OTHER       = 4294967295


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: SIP-Forking-Indication
; Section: 5.3.22
; Page: 47
SIP-Forking-Indication ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 523 10415 >
        SINGLE_DIALOGUE   = 0
        SEVERAL_DIALOGUES = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#sip-forking-indication-default)
; AVP: SIP-Forking-Indication
; Section: 5.3.22
; Page: 47
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"This is the default value applicable if the AVP is omitted."
    default SINGLE_DIALOGUE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#service-urn-prefix)
; AVP: Service-URN
; Section: 5.3.23
; Page: 48
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The string \"urn:service:\" in the beginning of the URN shall be omitted in the AVP and all subsequent text shall be included."
    text-only


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Acceptable-Service-Info
; Section: 5.3.24
; Page: 48
Acceptable-Service-Info ::= < AVP header: 526 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#vendor-id-acceptable-service-info)
      * [ Media-Component-Description ]
        [ Max-Requested-Bandwidth-DL ]
        [ Max-Requested-Bandwidth-UL ]
        [ Extended-Max-Requested-BW-DL ]
        [ Extended-Max-Requested-BW-UL ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Service-Info-Status
; Section: 5.3.25
; Page: 48
Service-Info-Status ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 527 10415 >
        "FINAL SERVICE INFORMATION"       = 0
        "PRELIMINARY SERVICE INFORMATION" = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#service-info-status-default)
; AVP: Service-Info-Status
; Section: 5.3.25
; Page: 48
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"If the Service-Info-Status AVP is not provided in the AA request, the value FINAL SERVICE INFORMATION shall be assumed."
    default "FINAL SERVICE INFORMATION"


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: AF-Signalling-Protocol
; Section: 5.3.26
; Page: 48
AF-Signalling-Protocol ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 529 10415 >
        NO_INFORMATION = 0
        SIP            = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#af-signalling-protocol-default)
; AVP: AF-Signalling-Protocol
; Section: 5.3.26
; Page: 48
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"If the AF-Signalling-Protocol AVP is not provided in the AA-Request, the value NO_INFORMATION shall be assumed."
    default NO_INFORMATION


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Sponsored-Connectivity-Data
; Section: 5.3.27
; Page: 49
Sponsored-Connectivity-Data ::= < AVP header: 530 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#vendor-id-sponsored-connectivity-data)
        [ Sponsor-Identity ]
        [ Application-Service-Provider-Identity ]
        [ Granted-Service-Unit ]
        [ Used-Service-Unit ]
        [ Sponsoring-Action ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-sponsored-connectivity-sponsor-identity)
; AVP: Sponsored-Connectivity-Data
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 5.3.27
; Page: 49
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The Sponsor-Identity AVP identifies the sponsor. It shall be included by the AF in the Sponsored-Connectivity-Data AVP except for the case of disabling sponsored data connectivity."
    absent-if not Sponsored-Connectivity-Data/Sponsor-Identity and not Sponsored-Connectivity-Data/Sponsoring-Action = DISABLE_SPONSORING
"The Application-Service-Provider-Identity AVP identifies the application service provider. It shall be included by the AF in the Sponsored-Connectivity-Data AVP except for the case of disabling sponsored data connectivity."
    absent-if not Sponsored-Connectivity-Data/Application-Service-Provider-Identity and not Sponsored-Connectivity-Data/Sponsoring-Action = DISABLE_SPONSORING


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#sponsored-connectivity-used-service-unit)
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Within: Sponsored-Connectivity-Data
; Section: 5.3.27
; Page: 49
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"Reporting shall be done, as requested by the AF, in CC-Total-Octets, CC-Input-Octets, CC-Output-Octets or CC-Time of the Used-Service-Unit AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Rx-Request-Type
; Section: 5.3.31
; Page: 49
Rx-Request-Type ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 533 10415 >
        INITIAL_REQUEST   = 0
        UPDATE_REQUEST    = 1
        PCSCF_RESTORATION = 2


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Required-Access-Info
; Section: 5.3.34
; Page: 50
Required-Access-Info ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 536 10415 >
        USER_LOCATION = 0
        MS_TIME_ZONE  = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#sharing-key-dl-sessions)
; AVP: Sharing-Key-DL
; Section: 5.3.37
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"If resource sharing applies between media components across AF sessions for the same user, the same value of the Sharing-Key-DL AVP shall be used;"
    text-only
"If resource sharing does not apply between media components across AF sessions for the same user, a different value of the Sharing-Key-DL AVP shall be used for each media component."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#sharing-key-ul-sessions)
; AVP: Sharing-Key-UL
; Section: 5.3.38
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"If resource sharing applies between media components across AF sessions for the same user, the same value of the Sharing-Key-UL AVP shall be used;"
    text-only
"If resource sharing does not apply between media components across AF sessions for the same user, a different value of the Sharing-Key-UL AVP shall be used for each media component."
    text-only


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Sponsoring-Action
; Section: 5.3.40
; Page: 51
Sponsoring-Action ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 542 10415 >
        DISABLE_SPONSORING = 0
        ENABLE_SPONSORING  = 1


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: Service-Authorization-Info
; Kind: bits
; Section: 5.3.46
; Table: 5.3.46
; Page: 52
"The transfer policy is known/unknown."                                    = 0
"The transfer policy has expired/has not expired"                          = 1
"The time window of the transfer policy has occurred/has not yet occurred" = 2


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Priority-Sharing-Indicator
; Section: 5.3.47
; Page: 52
Priority-Sharing-Indicator ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 550 10415 >
        PRIORITY_SHARING_ENABLED  = 0
        PRIORITY_SHARING_DISABLED = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#priority-sharing-indicator-default)
; AVP: Priority-Sharing-Indicator
; Section: 5.3.47
; Page: 52
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"This is the default value applicable if this AVP is not supplied."
    default PRIORITY_SHARING_DISABLED


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#media-component-status-default)
; AVP: Media-Component-Status
; Section: 5.3.48
; Page: 53
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"This is the default value applicable if this AVP is not supplied."
    default 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#content-version-unique)
; AVP: Content-Version
; Section: 5.3.49
; Page: 53
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The content version shall be unique for the content and for the lifetime of that content."
    text-only


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: AF-Requested-Data
; Kind: bits
; Section: 5.3.50
; Table: 5.3.50.1
; Page: 53
"EPC-level identities required" = 0


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: Pre-emption-Control-Info
; Kind: bits
; Section: 5.3.51
; Table: 5.3.51
; Page: 53
"Most recent added flow"  = 0
"Least recent added flow" = 1
"Highest bandwidth flow"  = 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#pre-emption-control-info-one-bit)
; AVP: Pre-emption-Control-Info
; Section: 5.3.51
; Page: 53
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The following values are defined, only one bit shall be set at the same time:"
    bits at-most-one 0 1 2


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: IMS-Content-Type
; Section: 5.3.61
; Page: 55
IMS-Content-Type ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 564 10415 >
        NO_CONTENT_DETAIL = 0
        CAT               = 1
        CONFERENCE        = 2


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Callee-Information
; Section: 5.3.62
; Page: 55
Callee-Information ::= < AVP header: 565 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#vendor-id-callee-information)
        [ Called-Party-Address ]
      * [ Requested-Party-Address ]
      * [ Called-Asserted-Identity ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#flus-identifier-prefix)
; AVP: FLUS-Identifier
; Section: 5.3.63
; Page: 55
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"It contains the string after \"a=label:\" starting with \"flus\" and may be followed by more characters as described in 3GPP TS 26.238 [69]."
    text-only


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: MA-Information
; Section: 5.3.66
; Page: 56
MA-Information ::= < AVP header: 570 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#vendor-id-ma-information)
        [ IP-CAN-Type ]
        [ RAT-Type ]
        [ MA-Information-Action ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#ma-information-action-default)
; AVP: MA-Information-Action
; Section: 5.3.67
; Page: 56
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"0 (ADD) is the default value."
    default 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#nid-digits)
; AVP: NID
; Section: 5.3.68
; Page: 56
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The NID AVP (AVP code 569) is of type OctetString, and it indicates Network Identifier (NID) consisting on 44 bits (11 hexadecimal digits), as specified in 3GPP TS 23.003 [38], clause 12.7."
    encoding element TS23.003 12.7.1 "NID"


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: 5GS-RAN-NAS-Release-Cause
; Section: 5.3.69
; Page: 56
5GS-RAN-NAS-Release-Cause ::= < AVP header: 572 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#vendor-id-5gs-ran-nas-release-cause)
        [ 5GMM-Cause ]
        [ 5GSM-Cause ]
        [ NGAP-Cause ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#5gmm-cause-coding)
; AVP: 5GMM-Cause
; Section: 5.3.70
; Page: 57
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AVP shall be coded as per the 5GMM Cause in clause 9.11.3.2 of 3GPP TS 24.501 [70]."
    encoding element TS24.501 9.11.3.2 "5GMM cause"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#5gsm-cause-coding)
; AVP: 5GSM-Cause
; Section: 5.3.71
; Page: 57
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The AVP shall be coded as per the 5GSM Cause in clause 9.11.4.2 of 3GPP TS 24.501 [70]."
    encoding element TS24.501 9.11.4.2 "5GSM cause"


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: NGAP-Cause
; Section: 5.3.72
; Page: 57
NGAP-Cause ::= < AVP header: 575 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#vendor-id-ngap-cause)
        { NGAP-Group }
        { NGAP-Value }


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#ngap-group-value)
; AVP: NGAP-Group
; Section: 5.3.73
; Page: 57
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The value of this IE shall equal to the ASN.1 value of the specified NGAP cause group"
    encoding element TS38.413 9.4.5 "Cause"


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Wireline-User-Location-Info
; Section: 5.3.75
; Page: 57
Wireline-User-Location-Info ::= < AVP header: 578 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.214.py#vendor-id-wireline-user-location-info)
        [ HFC-Node-Identifier ]
        [ GLI-Identifier ]
        [ Line-Type ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#wireline-user-location-info-members)
; AVP: Wireline-User-Location-Info
; Section: 5.3.75
; Page: 57
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The Wireline-User-Location-Info AVP (AVP code 578) is of type Grouped and contains either wireline Cable or wireline BBF user location information."
    members at-least-one HFC-Node-Identifier GLI-Identifier


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#wireline-user-location-info-hfc)
; AVP: HFC-Node-Identifier
; Within: Wireline-User-Location-Info
; Section: 5.3.75
; Page: 57
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The Wireline-User-Location-Info AVP (AVP code 578) is of type Grouped and contains either wireline Cable or wireline BBF user location information."
    excludes GLI-Identifier


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#wireline-user-location-info-line-type)
; AVP: Line-Type
; Within: Wireline-User-Location-Info
; Section: 5.3.75
; Page: 57
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The GLI-Identifier AVP indicates wireline BBF location and contains a Global Line Identifier. The Line-Type AVP indicates the type of line included in the GLI-Identifier AVP."
    requires GLI-Identifier


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#hfc-node-identifier-cablelabs)
; AVP: HFC-Node-Identifier
; Section: 5.3.76
; Page: 58
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The HFC-Node-Identifier AVP (AVP code 579) is of type OctetString and contains an HFC Node Identifier as specified in CableLabs WR-TR-5WWC-ARCH [73]."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#gli-identifier-base64)
; AVP: GLI-Identifier
; Section: 5.3.77
; Page: 58
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The GLI-Identifier AVP (AVP code 580) is of type OctetString and contains a Global Line Identifier (see clause 28.16.3 of 3GPP TS 23.003 [38]) encoded as base64-encoded characters, representing the GLI value (up to 150 bytes) as specified in BBF WT-470 [74]."
    encoding base64
    length *..200 octets


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: MPS-Action
; Section: 5.3.79
; Page: 58
MPS-Action ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 582 10415 >
        DISABLE_MPS_FOR_DTS                        = 0
        ENABLE_MPS_FOR_DTS                         = 1
        AUTHORIZE_AND_ENABLE_MPS_FOR_DTS           = 2
        AUTHORIZE_AND_ENABLE_MPS_FOR_AF_SIGNALLING = 3


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#user-location-info-coding)
; AVP: 3GPP-User-Location-Info
; Section: 5.4.0
; Table: 5.4.0.1
; Page: 59
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"Coding for type values between 0 and 134 shall be done as defined in 3GPP TS 29.274 [33]."
"Coding for these type values shall be done as defined in 3GPP TS 29.061 [34]"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#framed-ipv6-prefix-ue-address)
; AVP: Framed-IPv6-Prefix
; Section: 5.4.0
; Table: 5.4.0.1
; Page: 59
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The encoding of the value within this Octet String type AVP shall be as defined in RFC 3162 [20], clause 2.3. The \"Reserved\", \"Prefix-Length\" and \"Prefix\" fields shall be included in this order."
    encoding element RFC3162 2.3 "Framed-IPv6-Prefix"
"The AF shall set the \"Prefix Length\" to 128 and encode the Ipv6 address of the UE within the \"Prefix\" field."
    encoding element TS29.214 5.4.0 "Framed-IPv6-Prefix"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#sponsored-connectivity-granted-service-unit-members)
; AVP: Granted-Service-Unit
; Within: Sponsored-Connectivity-Data
; Section: 5.4.0
; Table: 5.4.0.1
; Page: 59
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"Only CC-Total-Octets, one of the CC-Input-Octets and CC-Output-Octets, or CC-Time AVPs are reused."
    members only CC-Total-Octets CC-Input-Octets CC-Output-Octets CC-Time


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#sponsored-connectivity-used-service-unit-members)
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Within: Sponsored-Connectivity-Data
; Section: 5.4.0
; Table: 5.4.0.1
; Page: 59
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"Only CC-Total-Octets, one of the CC-Input-Octets and CC-Output-Octets, or CC-Time AVPs are reused."
    members only CC-Total-Octets CC-Input-Octets CC-Output-Octets CC-Time


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#tos-traffic-class-mask)
; AVP: ToS-Traffic-Class
; Section: 5.4.0
; Table: 5.4.0.1
; Page: 59
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"The first octet contains the DSCP code and the second octet contains the mask field set to 11111100."
    length 2 octets
    bits set 2 3 4 5 6 7
    bits clear 0 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#user-equipment-info-imeisv)
; AVP: User-Equipment-Info
; Section: 5.4.0
; Table: 5.4.0.1
; Page: 59
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
