; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aar-supported-features-vendor)
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 5.4.1
; Page: 63
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"On the Rx reference point, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.214.dadx#aaa-initial-supported-features)
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 5.4.1
; Page: 63
; Versions: 18.4.0..19.3.0
"On the Rx reference point, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    text-only
"The following exceptions apply to the initial and stateless AAR/AAA command pair:"
"If the AAR command contains the Supported-Features AVP(s), the PCRF shall include the Supported-Features AVP(s) in the AAA command, with the ‘M’ bit cleared, indicating only the features that both the PCRF and AF support."
    present-if request/Rx-Request-Type = INITIAL_REQUEST and request/Supported-Features and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or request/Rx-Request-Type = PCSCF_RESTORATION and request/Supported-Features and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
"The following exceptions apply to the initial and stateless AAR/AAA command pair:"
"If the AAR command does not contain any Supported-Features AVP(s) and the PCRF supports Rel-7 Rx functionality, the AAA command shall not include the Supported-Features AVP."
    text-only


